    "body": "Some open questions I have:\n\n- What about this ties it to the `<template>` element (DSD in particular)? It seems like you could implement FACEs _without_ ShadowDOM, for example reimplementing `<input type=hidden>` as a FACE would not require a ShadowDOM. In that way perhaps this speaks more as a use case for Declarative Custom Element Definitions.\n- If we were to implement this (regardless of what the HTML syntax would look like), what would the value be for a custom element which never calls `setFormValue`? For example if the definition never loaded? Is there an intuitive answer here?",
