    "body": "> > The value would be you largely wouldn't have to think about the form\n> > associated APIs. You would kind of get it \"for free\" on simple components. (in my opinion)\n> \n> Sorry I meant more literally. What would `.value` be?\n\nA potentially naive question, but if the CE hasn't yet been defined, could the browser just ignore the shadow boundary and hoist the `<input>`, `<textarea>`, `<select>`,  and `<button type=\"submit\">` elements that are within the DSD to participate in the light DOM form. Everything remains encapsulated.\n\nAs long as a `name` attribute is present on the host, the `.value` would be accessible by the light DOM `<form>`, and you would just get all the expected basic form functionality, behaviour, values etc. \"for free\" as @KonnorRogers said. A button with type=\"submit\" wouldn't be required to have a name.\n\nI don't know the answer for if multiple inputs are in the DSD. Multiple name attributes on the individual form elements instead of host?\n\nOnce the element is upgraded, FACE would take over as it currently does. \n\n```html\n<form action=\"/submit.php\" method=\"POST\">\n    <my-input name=\"username\">\n        <template shadowrootmode=\"open\">\n            <label for=\"myInput\">Username</label>\n            <input id=\"myInput\" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"Username\" required>\n        </template>\n    </my-input>\n\n     <my-submit-button>\n         <template shadowrootmode=\"open\">\n             <button type=\"submit\">Next</button>\n          </template>\n     </my-submit-button>\n</form>\n```\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
