    "body": "> A potentially naive question, but if the CE hasn't yet been defined, could the browser just ignore the shadow boundary and hoist the `<input>`, `<textarea>`, `<select>`, and `<button type=\"submit\">` elements that are within the DSD to participate in the light DOM form. Everything remains encapsulated.\n\nthis is largely the behavior I _think_ I would desire. I don't mind ignore it once the host has \"connected\", and then my custom logic can take over.\n\n> Sorry I meant more literally. What would .value be?\n\nThis largely depends on behavior. will the host element be participating? or will it be just forwarding the shadow dom element?\n\nIf the host element is participating, then `.value` would be whatever the input value is.\nIf the shadow dom element is participating, then `.value` would be `null` until the host element connects and sets its own `.value`",
