    "body": "Revisiting this topic:\n\n> A potentially naive question, but if the CE hasn't yet been defined, could the browser just ignore the shadow boundary and hoist the `<input>`, `<textarea>`, `<select>`, and `<button type=\"submit\">` elements that are within the DSD to participate in the light DOM form. Everything remains encapsulated.\n\nFeels like this would need to be \"opt-in\" in some way as it would potentially break existing sites to always hoist. I imagine something similar to `referencetarget` could be a way forward here.",
