    "body": "Not sure if we're looking for API proposals here, but maybe something along the lines of `formControlReference` ?\n\n-  The `formControlReference` entry in the ShadowRootInit argument to `attachShadow()`.\n-  The `formControlReference` attribute on the ShadowRoot object.\n-  In HTML markup using the `shadowrootformcontrolreference` attribute on the `<template>` element.\n\n```js\nclass MyInput extends HTMLElement {\n  constructor() {\n        super();\n        this.shadowRoot = this.attachShadow({ \n          mode: \"closed\",\n          formControlReference: \"foo\",\n        });\n\n     this.shadowRoot.innerHTML = `<input id=\"foo\" name=\"${this.name}\">`\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```html\n<my-input>\n  <template shadowrootmode=\"open\" shadowrootformcontrolreference=\"foo\">\n    <input id=\"foo\" name=\"foo\">\n  </template>\n</my-input>\n```\n\nOnce the element is `:defined()` _and_ it is a `static formAssociated = true` then it should ignore the `formControlReference` (i think? maybe this is a way to not need all the boilerplate of form associated?)\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
